    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "the gray cast iron plate seen from 32 cm at its open end. Large threaded open bores fill the lower half and run off the left, right and bottom edges, and six rows of brass hex plugs on exposed threaded collars stand in the far rows against a warm seam.",
        "visual_consequence": "With the headline covered, a reader sees a plate where most of the holes stand empty and swallow light, while a smaller block far away is sealed with lit brass. That most went unanswered and a minority answered reads before any number.",
        "weakness": "The previous findings are fixed. In crops r3c1 and r3c2 the 3 o'clock rim notch is gone, and each near bore now shows a countersink ring and stepped thread crests lit warm on its far wall. In crops r2c1 and r2c2 the plugs have chamfered hex arrises, smooth domes, a visible threaded collar and a dark contact ring at the iron, and the pebbles near the dek are gone. Three minor items remain. The plate's far edge and its foot on the caliche are still not visible, because the rearmost plug row runs straight into the haze band. A faint lattice of thin dark lines shows on the iron between plug columns (r2c1, design x about 125 to 210, y about 730 to 810). The dome tops mirror the near black sky as dark caps. None of these stops the dominant subject reading as finished cast iron and brass at native or at feed size.",
        "repair": "Optional, for the panel. Lower the camera target slightly so the plate's far edge and its contact shadow on the caliche show as a thin dark line under the rearmost plugs.",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
        "feed_legible": true,
