        "subject": "the same plate seen from behind its answered end. About three rows of large brass hex plugs on threaded collars fill the lower third and run off the bottom edge, and threaded open bores recede to the plate's dark far edge against a warm caliche band.",
        "visual_consequence": "With the headline covered, a reader is left looking past a few sealed, lit plugs at a much larger field of open holes running away to the horizon. It is the cover turned around, so the unanswered majority is what the reader is left with.",
        "weakness": "The art is unchanged from the previous accepted reading. The broad hex faces are flat untextured tan, so close up the brass leans toward satin painted metal, and the bottom plug row sinks into the footer darkness. The rewritten dek runs four lines on the dark sky with no collision and reads in the thumb. Its place and its statement about the report must trace to c25 and c37.",
        "repair": "Optional, for the panel. Add a fine directional scratch normal and slight roughness variation to the hex flats so the broad faces break up their highlight like turned brass.",
