  "plan": {
    "hardest_frame": 2,
    "visual_argument": "One threaded bore for each of the 334 data center facilities in the Tribune's records, a brass plug in each of the 101 that returned the water board's survey and the 233 left open, so the count reads as light caught or swallowed before a word is read",
    "build_risk": "Frame 2 must read as cast iron hardware at feed size and never as the UI tray no. 59 shipped: 334 bores at 50 px pitch with thread rings, 101 brass hex plugs with domes, the plate's lit edge wall casting onto caliche, the carrier bleeding three edges and a cast fraction of 0.12 or more, all through TXBENCH.relief under the chassis light",
    "distinct_from_recent": "no. 57 was stair flights and a brass datum in a lastLight room and yard, no. 58 record cards, wristbands and a card drawer in lastLight, no. 59 a floodlit plant apron and bays with bluebonnet tape. This deck is a single cast iron plate and a water tank outdoors on caliche, with a dust brass accent and no building interior"
  },
